      },
      "statement": "Let X,Y be arbitrary measurable spaces, μ,ν arbitrary measures and f:X→Y measure preserving (measurable and f₊μ=ν). Let M_f:L²(ν;ℝ)→L²(μ;ℝ) be canonical isometric pullback. Then its range is exactly the submodule of L²(μ;ℝ) classes having an AE strongly measurable representative for the comap sigma algebra f⁻¹ΣY. There is no probability, finite-measure, standard-Borel or finite-dimensional hypothesis.",
      "assumptions": [
        "Let X,Y be arbitrary measurable spaces, μ,ν arbitrary measures and f:X→Y measure preserving (measurable and f₊μ=ν). Let M_f:L²(ν;ℝ)→L²(μ;ℝ) be canonical isometric pullback."
      ],
      "formulae": [
        {
          "label": "Exact range of real L2 pullback",
          "tex": "\\operatorname{ran}M_f=L^2(f^{-1}\\Sigma_Y,\\mu;\\mathbb R),\\quad M_fu=u\\circ f."
        }
      ],
